    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0141" n="137" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1660: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-10T17:00:00-04:00">August 10, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>482. Your 1070, August 5, 6 p.m., in regard to Chinese terrorist.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Your 1042, July 28, 10 p.m.,<anchor n="83" xml:id="d155-f1"/> reported
                        that the Chinese in question “was handed over to the Japanese authorities.”
                        Your 1070 states that you are informed that the action of the Shanghai
                        Municipal authorities was based on paragraph 6 of the proclamation quoted in
                        your 992, July 14, 6 p.m.<anchor n="82" xml:id="d155-f2"/> That paragraph
                        provides merely for the expulsion from the Settlement of persons referred to
                        therein.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>So far as the record available to the Department is concerned the action
                        of the Municipal authorities was not in accordance with their own
                        regulations and the Department would appreciate your comment upon this
                        apparent discrepancy.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
